  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...\n\nWinds will become southwesterly today. This will allow \ntemperatures to warm considerably, with even more warming by\nThursday. Afternoon readings by Thursday will be in the 80s for\nall but the higher elevations. \n\n\nKEY MESSAGE 2...\n\nA cold front will push southward through the region on Friday, \nbringing showers and thunderstorms. Models show the front \nstalling south of the region Friday night. The area will remain\nclose enough to the front however, that some rain or drizzle\nwill remain possible on Saturday, more likely over southern West\nVirginia and southwest Virginia. \n\nAn upper level wave will move across the area on Sunday,\nenhancing the chances of precipitation. Once again, this will \nbe more likely over southern West Virginia and southwest \nVirginia. This system will also push the cold front further\nsouth, leaving dry weather for the beginning of the next work\nweek.",
